From 2280bf4316c1b3edbd730d09968c2d737e4749de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:50:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 52/73] pco: back-propagate pixel output writes again

try_back_prop_instr returned early for pixout destinations, ahead of the
checks written for them (no alphaf/depthf in between, pixout not already
a source of the producer). So every fragment shader ended with an extra
mbyp into the output register. Let those checks decide instead; the last
ALU op (e.g. the u8888 pack) now writes the output register directly.

vkrender fragment shader 8 -> 7 groups. vkedge (MSAA, helper
invocations, blending), vkrender pixel checks and output hashes pass;
the discard probes behave exactly as before.
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c
index b9aedea..fac4293 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c
@@ -263,7 +263,6 @@ static inline bool try_back_prop_instr(struct pco_use *uses, pco_instr *instr)
 
    if (pco_ref_is_reg(*pdest_from) &&
        pco_ref_get_reg_class(*pdest_from) == PCO_REG_CLASS_PIXOUT) {
-      return false;
 
       bool has_isp_fb = false;
 
